# ── Chapter 30 fidelity pins: "When the System Notices It Broke" ─────────────
#
# The justice-specific continuation is also exercised by:
#   tests/pins/justice/defect/downstream-withdrawal-and-fresh-correction/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/defect/wrong-version-cannot-withdraw-real-relief/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/nonresponse/positive/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/nonresponse/silence-without-positive-elapsed-evidence/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/justice/appeal/request-without-operator-or-previous-permission/expect.pins.nibli
#
# "When the finding itself turns out to be wrong" rests on these
# actual-constitution withdrawal sequences:
#   tests/pins/knowledge/free-field/restriction-defect-and-rights-sequence/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/free-field/unrelated-defect/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/record-power/power/holding-defect-and-rights-sequence/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/record-power/power/unrelated-defect/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/priority/false-scarcity-stops-the-allocation/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/scarcity/priority/not-a-shortage-BudgetChoice/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/knowledge/free-field/restriction-does-not-travel-between-fields/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/record-power/power/holding-does-not-cover-another-subject/expect.pins.nibli
# Each asserts a reviewed defect and withdraws the affected permission while
# protective duties and the person's standing, floor and ballot remain. These
# sequences do not establish that any correction was made or published.
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/30-when-the-system-notices-it-broke.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # all substantive cases and contradiction checks
#
# The old unread-duty endpoint is retired. Existing two-place Review and Appeals
# duties must feed the exact typed three-place consumer, and `obliged` remains a
# derived conclusion rather than a writable verdict. Both are exact-one source
# preconditions because a duplicate consumer or declaration is also a defect.
#
# Positive custody-condition findings have their own case, place, period and
# independent witnesses. Missing company evidence is not an isolation finding.
# Routine custody review and complaint access do not wait for such a finding.
# The complete condition and explicit weaker-rule cases are in:
#   tests/pins/custody/condition-findings/expect.pins.nibli
#   tests/pins/custody/condition-findings/counterfactual.pins.nibli

# WHAT FALSE MEANS HERE — three kinds, and only one is a verdict. A FALSE on a
# corpus name this KB never mentions is real but empty: nothing could have made
# it TRUE. A non-corpus name is not a FALSE at all — the run aborts, pins not
# trustworthy. And a well-formed query on an argument its relation never
# carries is a vacuous green that passes forever. Article 0a closed the
# ASSERTION side only — a widening fact now aborts the run instead of loading —
# but a QUERY on an unmentioned name still answers a clean FALSE, so kind one
# is untouched. Pin a FALSE only where the KB could have said TRUE, and say in
# the comment what would flip it.

# The ecological and animal continuation moved with its prose to the chapter on
# who owes and what follows; its probe lives in that chapter's pin file now.
:expect-pins 37

# The source-bound finding/action contract consumes the older underfilled duty
# only after the supplied initial-finding standard and its other typed evidence
# have rejoined. The result is a formal duty, never proof that anybody acted.
:require test "$(grep -F -c '& obliged($reader, $subject) -> obliged($reader, $reader_duty, $reader_standard).' book-1/source/constitution.nibli)" -eq 1
:require test "$(grep -F -c 'derived_only("obliged").' book-1/source/constitution.nibli)" -eq 1

# None of these missing company receipts is positive evidence of isolation.
# Keep every prior case, now as an ordinary negative regression.
? err(Adam, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Hano, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Lalo, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Nando, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Faro, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Kel, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Ruk, Isolation).
# => FALSE

# Relief and protected disclosures are not condition reports either.
? err(Nia, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Iris, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Lior, Isolation).
# => FALSE

# "Ask which free people are, and the answer is none."
? err(Bela, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Jala, Isolation).
# => FALSE

# The shipped record supplies no matching company receipt for either case.
? meets(Hano).
# => FALSE

? meets(Bela).
# => FALSE

# [v0.9] the placement marker, repaired: it reads a placement report against
# derived eligibility, and the record holds no reports — so it is silent about
# Ruk and Lalo, whom the old rule flagged while they were correctly placed.
# Dormant is not blind: chapter 28's closing probes show it firing on a
# reported misplacement.
? err(Ruk, Placement).
# => FALSE

? err(Lalo, Placement).
# => FALSE

? err(Hano, Placement).
# => FALSE

# and Ruk is correctly placed — under the old marker that was what made the
# alarm wrong; under the repaired one there is nothing to report
? building(HighSec, Ruk).
# => TRUE

# Routine custody review is owed without an isolation or placement finding.
? obliged(Review, Ruk).
# => TRUE

? obliged(Review, Lalo).
# => TRUE

# The automatic review duty also reaches these custodial cases.
? obliged(Review, Adam).
# => TRUE

? obliged(Review, Hano).
# => TRUE

# THE ARGUMENT-ORDER DISCRIMINATOR — DO NOT DROP EITHER HALF. Writing the duty
# backwards leaves the four pins above TRUE while silently meaning the PRISONER is
# bound to the Review. These two are the only thing that tells the versions apart.
# [2026-07-31] The typo route closed upstream — `obligated` was renamed
# `obligated_by`, so that spelling no longer compiles. The converse mechanism
# survives under the new name, and a slip within `obliged` itself was never
# covered by anything but these two lines.
? obliged(Ruk, Review).
# => FALSE

? obliged(Adam, Review).
# => FALSE

# silent where the markers are silent: Bela is not confined, Dara is shielded.
? obliged(Review, Bela).
# => FALSE

? obliged(Review, Dara).
# => FALSE

# "Several of the judged are not held" — Dara is the newest of them and was
# missing from the roster above, which is how a count in the prose went stale.
? err(Dara, Isolation).
# => FALSE

# ── the exhibit: what else was available and was not built ───────────────────
# MUST BE LAST. An accepted rule loads into the KB and stays; any query after
# this point is measuring a polluted base. rights-floor.pins.nibli:285 records a
# real vacuous green from forgetting exactly this.
#
# MUST BE LAST is now a choice rather than the only option: nibli 425567b added
# `:accept-scoped`, which retracts the statement afterwards and so cannot
# pollute. It was tried here and refused — the rule is the premise of the query
# below it, and scoped, the accept still passes as loadable while
# `err(Ruk, Duty)` flips to FALSE (measured 2026-08-01). Scoping would keep the
# half of the chapter's claim that the stratifier permits this rule and lose the
# half that says it derives.
#
# "The design could mark the review body for having ignored the duty; that rule
#  was tried and it works." This is that rule. It makes err and obliged mutually
# recursive over positive edges and the stratifier permits it, which is why the
# chapter can no longer call the powerlessness structural.
:accept
all $x: obliged(Review, $x) & ~capture(Review, $x) -> err($x, Duty).

? err(Ruk, Duty).
# => TRUE

# ── The child with nobody ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The birth-only fixture supplies no positive condition finding or placement
# report. No custodial review duty follows from the birth entry alone.
? err(Nell, Isolation).
# => FALSE

? err(Nell, Placement).
# => FALSE

# These particular markers do not reach the birth-only fixture.
? prisoner(Nell).
# => FALSE

? obliged(Review, Nell).
# => FALSE

# "Run it against this child in a counterfactual and it does fire" — that run is
# tests/pins/records/child_with_nobody/undelivered.pins.nibli, against the base
# counterfactual/undelivered-marker. Here, on the shipped source, the marker
# does not exist; the ordinary floor and assistance duties remain separate.
? owe(State, Eats, Nell).
# => TRUE

? eats(Nell).
# => FALSE
